node_modules/
# Secrets: ignore every .env variant (e.g. .env.safebeauty) but keep the template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.firebase/
# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored. `npm ci` requires it, and
# without it every install resolves whatever versions happen to be current —
# so CI would test different code than production runs.

# The two project env files hold no secrets — a vendor API base URL and this
# app's own hosting URL — and a clean checkout cannot deploy without them, which
# is a deploy step that lives outside the repository (specification 10.4). Real
# secrets stay in Secret Manager via defineSecret and are never written here.
!.env.safebeauty
!.env.safebeauty-staging
